--- body ---
## Context

Author asked directly: "Are we testing against the ticket 029 gold adversarial
library?" No -- every adversarial test in this wave (0690, 0695) runs against
synthetic host mocks in a Node `vm` sandbox. None of them exercise the sitter
against real pathological documents: multi-hundred-page books, mixed scripts
(the Menagerie's EN/FR/VI MUST tier plus SHOULD-tier Arabic/Russian/Chinese/
German/Hindi/Spanish), malformed or oversized attachments, or group-library
membership. Mock tests prove the scheduler's control flow; they cannot prove
the census/extraction pipeline survives what the corpus was specifically
built to contain.

Ticket 0029 is the tracker for that corpus; its child 0632 ("the harness
triplet") is what actually produces a live, injectable fixture library, and
is itself currently blocked on a real question (a dedicated public Zotero
group with linked-file attachments -- the only group this host belongs to is
a live 13,560-item research library, not a fixture target, and Zotero has no
group-creation API). This ticket cannot start before 0632 unblocks; it exists
now so the sitter's validation isn't forgotten once it does.

## Work

- Once 0632 delivers an injectable fixture library, run the sitter's full
  census -> candidate -> extraction -> accounting pipeline against it in a
  real (or realistic-scale) Zotero profile.
- Specifically watch for: a census that never terminates or takes
  disproportionately long on the corpus's largest documents; extraction
  hangs or crashes on any SHOULD-tier script; the 0699 accounting fix
  (every non-indexed document lands in exactly one bucket) actually holding
  on documents that fail for real reasons, not synthetic ones; group-library
  attachments handled correctly by the admission/inspection logic.
- This is an integration/acceptance validation, not a unit-test replacement
  -- it does not retire or duplicate 0690/0695's mock-based tests.

## Acceptance

- [ ] Sitter runs a full census+extraction pass over the live Menagerie
      fixture without hanging or crashing.
- [ ] Final failure/success counts reconcile against the corpus's known
      document count (ties to 0699's reconciliation test, on real data).
- [ ] Any script/format that the sitter cannot handle is named explicitly,
      not silently miscounted or dropped.
